nce for `FileProvider`, but `FileProvider.getUriForFile` requires the file to **exist**. If it doesn't exist on disk yet, `FileProvider` will throw. `TakePicture()` contract typically requires an empty file to write into.\n- **OCR \"Apply All\" behavior (Lines 498-505):** When `selectedFields.isEmpty()` but `result.recognizedNumbers.isNotEmpty()`, the button says \"Применить все\" but the code only iterates `selectedFields` (which is empty) — **no fields are actually applied**. The user thinks they applied all values but nothing happens.\n\n## 18. SalaryCalculatorViewModel.kt\n**Issues:**\n- **Context in ViewModel (Line 13):** `private val context: Context` — anti-pattern. The ViewModel holds a direct reference to a `Context` (potentially an Activity). Should use `Application` context. Koin's `get()` resolves `Context` as the Application context, so it's *likely* safe, but not guaranteed.\n- **Salary calculation business logic in ViewModel (Line 183+):** Hard-coded financial constants (tax rates, base salary, etc.) should be in a configuration/repository, not buried in the ViewModel.\n\n## 19. SalaryModels.kt\n**Issues:**\n- **No validation on deserialization (Lines 30-39):** `getRecords()` uses `toDoubleOrNull()` correctly, but month names with `|` characters would break the parsing format.\n- **CSV injection risk (Line 69):** Month names are written directly to CSV without sanitization. If a month name contained `;` or `\"`, the CSV would be malformed.\n\n## 20. SalaryPdfExporter.kt\n**Issues:** ✅ Clean.\n\n## 21. ScheduleExport.kt\n**Issues:**\n- **Missing try-catch (Line 37):** `context.startActivity(shareIntent)` will throw `ActivityNotFoundException` if no app handles `ACTION_SEND`. Should wrap in try-catch.\n\n## 22. ScheduleExportDialog.kt\n**Issues:** ✅ Clean. Good use of coroutine + background dispatching.\n\n## 23. ScheduleImageExporter.kt\n**Issues:**\n- **High memory usage for year image (Line 197-200):** Even with `tileScale = 0.5f` and `RGB_565`, 12 months are processed sequentially. Each `createMonthImage()` allocates a full 1400×1900 ARGB_8888 bitmap (~10 MB) before downscaling — peak memory during loop is ~30 MB (full + scaled + canvas). On low-memory devices this could still trigger OOM.\n- **`canvas.drawColor(Color.WHITE)` (Line 191):** Uses `android.graphics.Color.WHITE` (int), while the rest of the code uses `ExportStyle.PAPER` — inconsistent, though functionally identical.\n\n## 24. ScheduleScreen.kt\n**Issues:**\n- **Deprecated API usage (Lines 7, 34, 216):** `@OptIn(ExperimentalFoundationApi::class)` — `HorizontalPager` was promoted to stable in Compose Foundation 1.6.0. The opt-in annotation is no longer needed if the project uses Compose 1.6+.\n- **`SettingsManager.setBrigade(num)` called on every chip click (Line 143):** This also triggers `ShiftWidgetProvider.triggerUpdate(context)` inside, plus `ShiftWidgetProvider` reads brigade from `\"settings\"` SharedPrefs with key `\"brigade\"` — but `SettingsManager` uses `\"alarm_settings\"` prefs with key `\"selected_brigade\"`. **The widget reads from a DIFFERENT SharedPreferences file and key** — the widget will always show brigade 1 regardless of the user's selection.\n\n## 25. SettingsManager.kt\n**Issues:**\n- **Widget prefs mismatch (Line 94-98):** `setBrigade()` calls `ShiftWidgetProvider.triggerUpdate(context)`, which sends a broadcast. But `ShiftWidgetProvider.updateWidget()` reads `prefs.getInt(\"brigade\", 1)` from prefs file `\"settings\"`, while `SettingsManager` stores the brigade in `\"alarm_settings\"` with key `\"selected_brigade\"`. **Bug: Widget always shows brigade 1.**\n\n## 26. SettingsScreen.kt\n**Issues:**\n- **MediaPlayer never nullified on dispose (Lines 58-63):** The `DisposableEffect` releases `currentMediaPlayer`, but `mediaPlayer` variable still holds the (now-released) reference. If user navigates back to Settings, `isPlaying` is still `true` but the player is released — clicking play would use a released player.\n- **Duplicate `CompactColorRow` / `ColorSelectorRow` composables (Lines 586-623):** These two functions are 100% identical — pure code duplication.\n\n## 27. ShiftSchedule.kt\n**Issues:**\n- **Anchor date is 2026-01-01 (Line 9):** The schedule calculation only works correctly from this date. If the app is used before 2026, `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between()` returns a negative value. The modulo fixup (Lines 54-56) handles negative indices correctly, so dates before 2026 produce valid but possibly wrong results — the schedule was designed for 2026 onward.\n\n## 28. ShiftType.kt\n**Issues:**\n- **Unused import (Line 4):** `java.time.LocalTime` — actually used (for `startTime`/`endTime`), not unused. ✅ Clean.\n\n## 29. ShiftWidgetProvider.kt\n**Issues:**\n- **🔴 CRITICAL BUG (Lines 54-55):** \n  ```kotlin\n  val prefs = context.getSharedPreferences(\"settings\", Context.MODE_PRIVATE)\n  val brigade = prefs.getInt(\"brigade\", 1)\n  ```\n  The app stores brigade in prefs file `\"alarm_settings\"` under key `\"selected_brigade\"` (see `SettingsManager` + `PreferenceKeys`), but the widget reads from file `\"settings\"` under key `\"brigade\"`. **The widget always shows brigade 1**, ignoring the user's actual selection.\n\n## 30. SilentModeReceiver.kt\n**Issues:**\n- **Main thread SharedPreferences + AlarmScheduler (Line 32):** Constructing `AlarmScheduler` and calling `updateAutoSilenceAlarms()` synchronously in `onReceive()` — same ANR risk as other BroadcastReceivers.\n- **No `goAsync()` (unlike BootReceiver):** The receiver does synchronous work (SharedPreferences read + alarm rescheduling) without calling `goAsync()`, increasing ANR risk.\n- **Inconsistent silent mode strategy (Lines 47-65):** For API < 23, it uses `AudioManager.ringerMode`, but for API >= 23 it uses `NotificationManager.interruptionFilter`. These are different systems — setting ringer mode to silent doesn't affect DND, and vice versa. The fallback on older devices may not actually silence notifications.\n\n## 31. SplashActivity.kt\n**Issues:**\n- **Deprecated API (Line 96):** `overridePendingTransition(android.R.anim.fade_in, android.R.anim.fade_out)` is deprecated in API 34+. Should use `overrideActivityTransition()` on API 34+.\n\n## 32. di/AppModule.kt\n**Issues:** ✅ Clean.\n\n## 33. ui/theme/Color.kt\n**Issues:**\n- **Unused file:** None of `Purple80`, `PurpleGrey80`, `Pink80`, `Purple40`, `PurpleGrey40`, `Pink40` are referenced anywhere outside `Theme.kt`. The entire file is dead code if `Theme.kt` is also unused.\n\n## 34. ui/theme/Theme.kt\n**Issues:**\n- **Unused composable:** `SalarynaftanTheme` is **never called** anywhere in the app. `MainActivity` uses `MaterialTheme(colorScheme = colorScheme)` directly. The entire `ui/theme/` package is dead code.\n\n## 35. ui/theme/Type.kt\n**Issues:**\n- **Unused file:** `Typography` is referenced only from `Theme.kt`, which is itself unused. Dead code.\n\n---\n\n# Summary of Critical/High-Impact Bugs\n\n| # | Severity | File | Issue |\n|---|----------|------|-------|\n| 1 | 🔴 **Critical** | `ShiftWidgetProvider.kt:54-55` | Widget reads from wrong SharedPreferences file/key — always shows brigade 1 |\n| 2 | 🟠 **High** | `SalaryCalculatorScreen.kt:498` | OCR \"Apply All\" button appears to work but actually applies nothing |\n| 3 | 🟠 **High** | `OcrSalaryScanner.kt:33` | TextRecognizer never closed — native memory leak |\n| 4 | 🟠 **High** | `AlarmReceiver.kt:72-89` | Heavy synchronous work in BroadcastReceiver risks ANR |\n| 5 | 🟡 **Medium** | `ScheduleExport.kt:37` | Missing try-catch on `startActivity` → crash if no handler |\n| 6 | 🟡 **Medium** | `SalaryCalculatorScreen.kt:96` | Photo file for FileProvider may not exist on disk |\n| 7 | 🟡 **Medium** | `AlarmsTabScreen.kt:120,348` | Regular alarm list not recomposing after mutations |\n| 8 | 🟡 **Medium** | `SilentModeReceiver.kt` | No `goAsync()` despite synchronous I/O in `onReceive()` |\n| 9 | 🔵 **Low** | `ui/theme/*.kt` (3 files) | Entire `ui/theme/` package is dead code — neve